  "summary_en": "US FDA regulation (21 CFR Part 890) classifying physical medicine devices into Classes I–III, with premarket notification exemptions and special controls. Includes powered exoskeletons, powered upper-extremity prostheses, EEG-driven exercisers and powered wheelchairs, requiring safety, software, and clinical testing and labeling.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Classifies physical medicine devices into Class I, II, III with premarket notification (510(k)) exemptions limited by §890.9",
   "Powered lower extremity exoskeletons are Class II with special controls: mechanical, EMC, software hazard analysis, clinical testing, training, labeling",
   "Advanced powered upper extremity prostheses are Class II with testing of safeguards, force sensors, and software validation",
   "EEG-driven upper extremity powered exerciser is Class II with clinical and software verification requirements",
   "Class III premarket approval applies to certain diathermy and rigid pneumatic orthosis devices"
  ],
